        "message": "fix(23): the same continuation trap, a third time — caught by the sweep before CI\n\nThe toolchain comment block I added in 816d27f landed INSIDE the cmake\ninvocation, between its continuation lines:\n\n    cmake -S src-llama -B build \\\n      # THE NDK'S OWN TOOLCHAIN FILE, NOT A HAND-WRITTEN ONE.\n      ...\n      -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=...\n\nwhich is the identical defect fixed in 5f8e6f1 and reintroduced in cd4e50b. This\ntime the repo-wide sweep caught it in the same command that made it, before a run\nwas dispatched:\n\n    traps: 0\n\nand the command is verified by parsing the YAML and asserting no '#' appears\nbetween 'cmake -S' and '-G Ninja':\n\n    --- comment-free continuation: OK ---\n\nThree occurrences of one mistake is enough to stop treating the lint as\nadvisory. The sweep now runs in the same shell invocation as every workflow edit,\nnot as a separate step someone can forget.",
